      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I found that VRChat discarded changes to layers 22-31 which reset them to their original names. Setting the culling mask does indeed work and is not bugged.\n\nhttps://creators.vrchat.com/worlds/layers/ specifies:\n\n\"Layers 22-31 are unused 'User' Unity layers. You can edit them freely, and changes to these layers will not be discarded when you build & upload your world.\"\n\nSo this is either a bug that needs to be fixed, or the documentation corrected to specify that even Layer 22-31 changes will be discarded on upload.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2026-02-08T01:28:49.552Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "https://creators.vrchat.com/worlds/udon/vrc-graphics/vrc-camera-settings/ specifies LayerMask CullingMask as exposed to Udon in both read and write for ScreenCamera, but doesn't seem to work in live.\n\n1. Create a simple UdonSharp script for changing the layer mask. The script will compile successfully and will not throw any errors (Ensure the specified layers are not reserved and their number is higher or equal to 23.):\n\nprivate void SetScreenCamLayersVisibility(bool visible)\n\n{\n\n    int layerMask = LayerMask.GetMask(\"Tanks\", \"Structures\");\n\n    int currentMask = VRCCameraSettings.ScreenCamera.CullingMask;\n\n    int newMask = visible ? (currentMask | layerMask) : (currentMask & ~layerMask);\n\n    VRCCameraSettings.ScreenCamera.CullingMask = newMask;\n\n}\n\n2. Test in Unity play mode, the method will successfully hide and show objects on specified layers.\n\n3. Upload to VRChat. Testing live both in desktop and VR mode (Windows) the method silently fails to change the ScreenCamera culling mask. No errors are thrown.",
